Subject: [R-pkg-team] Bug#916427: ITP: r-cran-magick -- advanced graphics
 and image-processing in GNU R
Message-ID: <154478564409.16712.13118612997844600462.reportbug@mail.an3as.eu>

Package: wnpp
Severity: wishlist
Owner: Andreas Tille <tille at debian.org>

* Package name    : r-cran-magick
  Version         : 2.0
  Upstream Author : Jeroen Ooms
* URL             : https://cran.r-project.org/package=magick
* License         : MIT
  Programming Lang: GNU R
  Description     : advanced graphics and image-processing in GNU R
 Bindings to 'ImageMagick': the most comprehensive open-source image
 processing library available. Supports many common formats (png, jpeg, tiff,
 pdf, etc) and manipulations (rotate, scale, crop, trim, flip, blur, etc).
 All operations are vectorized via the Magick++ STL meaning they operate either
 on a single frame or a series of frames for working with layers, collages,
 or animation. In RStudio images are automatically previewed when printed to
 the console, resulting in an interactive editing environment. The latest
 version of the package includes a native graphics device for creating
 in-memory graphics or drawing onto images using pixel coordinates.

Remark: This package is maintained by Debian R Packages Maintainers at
   https://salsa.debian.org/r-pkg-team/r-cran-magick
This package is needed to upgrade r-cran-animation to its latest upstream version.


